---
title: Roasted Pepper Gazpacho
servings: 4
course: Starter
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Quarter, deseed and slice the @red peppers{3}. Heat the @olive oil{3%tbsp} in a large pan and sauté the @shallots{4}(chopped), @thyme{1%sprig}, @bay leaf{1%small} and @garlic{1%clove}(crushed) without colouring until soft. Add the peppers and @basil{3%sprigs}(including stalks) and cook on a high heat for about ~{5%minutes}, until the pepper soften.

Then turn the heat down, cover the pan, and cook slowly for 10 to ~{15%minutes}, stirring occasionally.

Take off the heat and add the @plum tomatoes, very ripe{7}(chopped, seeds remaining), @tomato passata{800%ml}, @salt and @black pepper{}. Leave to marinate overnight if you can.

Remove all the herbs and blend the soup in a food processor until smooth. Add the @double cream{100%ml}, @Tabasco sauce{few drops} and @tomato purée{1%tbsp} and blend again briefly. Pass the soup through a fine sieve and adjust the seasoning. Chill well before serving.

> This soup improves with age, so you can eat it over the next couple of days and it will only get better.